      "message": "psbt: accept taproot ALL sigs with sighash unset\n\nSignPSBTInput() assumes SIGHASH_DEFAULT for a taproot input when\nneither PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE nor the caller's sighash_type is set.\nIts check of existing signatures then rejected every 65-byte\ntaproot signature, so a PSBT holding a valid SIGHASH_ALL signature\ncould be neither finalized nor signed further.\n\nWhen neither the field nor the parameter is set, the default is only\nassumed, so also accept a 65-byte signature ending in SIGHASH_ALL.\nNONE, SINGLE and ANYONECANPAY variants are still rejected, as are\nall mismatches when the field or the parameter is set.\n\nFixes #36507.",
